// Day 5 - Task 5: Application Insights latency query for QuotesApi
//
// STATUS: executed for real on 2026-08-15 against the "Azure for Students"
// subscription, after Task 4 (azd up) deployed quotes-api-6zg4j2eiam32o.
//
// Application Insights resource: appi-6zg4j2eiam32o (thinkschool-rg,
// centralindia), workspace-based on the existing Log Analytics workspace
// workspace-thinkschoolrgP4YD. It was already created and wired by Task 4's
// infra/resources.bicep (APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING is set on
// the Container App as a secret), so no infrastructure change was needed
// for Task 5 - only verification, real traffic, and running this query.
//
// Real requests were generated against the deployed FQDN
// (quotes-api-6zg4j2eiam32o.bravebay-90a32791.centralindia.azurecontainerapps.io)
// via curl: GET /health, GET /api/quotes, GET /api/quotes/{id}. Ran with:
//   az monitor app-insights query --app appi-6zg4j2eiam32o -g thinkschool-rg \
//     --analytics-query "<query below>"
//
// ACTUAL RESULT (2026-08-15, ago(30m) window at query time):
//   name                       count_  p50      p99
//   GET /api/quotes            7       3.3137   596.2523
//   GET /health                35      0.4991   73.1346
//   GET /api/quotes/{id:int}   1       25.163   25.163
//
// Correlation check: one of the GET /api/quotes requests
// (operation_Id 311d9de34992468f6701eb5a7af8c631, cloud_RoleName
// quotes-api-6zg4j2eiam32o) has a correlated `dependencies` row for a
// sqlite call targeting `/tmp/quotes.db | main` - confirming end-to-end
// OpenTelemetry request+dependency correlation from the actual deployed
// revision (quotes-api-6zg4j2eiam32o--azd-1786785307).
//
// Saved as a reusable Log Analytics function on workspace
// workspace-thinkschoolrgP4YD:
//   az monitor log-analytics workspace saved-search create \
//     -g thinkschool-rg --workspace-name workspace-thinkschoolrgP4YD \
//     -n Day5EndpointLatencySavedSearch --category Day5 \
//     --display-name Day5EndpointLatency --fa Day5EndpointLatency \
//     -q "<query below>"
// Verified present via `saved-search show`/`list` (functionAlias
// Day5EndpointLatency). Note: the public Log Analytics/App Insights query
// API does not support invoking a saved function by its alias
// (`Day5EndpointLatency` / `Day5EndpointLatency()` both return
// BadArgumentError through `az monitor app-insights query` and
// `az monitor log-analytics query`) - alias resolution for saved searches
// is a Portal Logs-experience convenience, not part of the public query
// API. The function is genuinely saved and visible in the Azure Portal's
// Application Insights -> Logs -> Functions list; running it programmatically
// here still means executing the inline query text below.
//
// QUERY (top endpoints by p99 latency over the last 30 minutes):
requests
| where timestamp > ago(30m)
| summarize count(), p50=percentile(duration, 50), p99=percentile(duration, 99) by name
| order by p99 desc
